 "final_text_tail": "I've found the likely cause. For rows whose group key is NaN, the label is -1. When no mask is passed, which is the case for datetimelike data viewed as int64, the Cython kernels hit `elif lab < 0: continue` and skip the row. That leaves `out` unset for those rows instead of writing NaT.\n\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/_libs/groupby.pyx\", \"pandas/core/groupby/ops.py\"], \"functions\": [\"group_cumsum\", \"group_cummin_max\", \"group_rank\", \"WrappedCythonOp._call_cython_op\", \"group_cumprod\"]}",
